From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] svcs: build without libzonecfg

TIER 4 -- NOT UPSTREAMABLE, KEEP LOCAL. This is a bring-up shim, not a fix.
It removes a (small) feature to avoid a dependency chain, and upstream should
not take it as written: a real submission would wire `HAVE_LIBZONECFG` to a
build-time knob and *default it on*, so a normal gate build is unchanged and
only an explicitly reduced configuration opts out. Here the macro is simply
never defined. Same shape, and the same reasoning, as patch 0016
(`svc.startd: build without libbe and libfmevent`).

`svcs` links `-lzonecfg` for exactly one symbol. Every zone-shaped thing in
`svcs.c` and `explain.c` -- `getzoneid`, `getzonenamebyid`, `ZONENAME_MAX`,
`GLOBAL_ZONEID` -- comes from libc and <zone.h>. The one libzonecfg call is
`zone_get_rootpath()`, at `svcs.c:477`, reached only from
`pg_get_single_val()` and only when all of the following hold: a zone was
named with `-z`/`-Z`, the property being read is `SCF_PROPERTY_LOGFILE` or
`SCF_PROPERTY_ALT_LOGFILE`, and the read succeeded. Its whole effect is
cosmetic, and the comment above it says so: "As a convenience, we're going to
prepend the zone path to the name of the log file."

So what is given up is precisely the log-path prefixing of `svcs -z <zone>
-L`. With the guard off, the log file is reported by its path *within* the
zone rather than as seen from the global zone. On a system with no
`zoneadm`, no configured zones and no way to create one, that is not a
reachable code path at all: `g_zonename` can only become non-NULL via `-z`
or `-Z`, and `-Z` already requires being in the global zone with zones to
enumerate.

What it buys is the entire libzonecfg dependency chain, seven packages that
would otherwise have to be built before `svcs` could exist at all:

  * libbrand   -- libxml2, libc
  * librcm     -- libc, libnvpair
  * libvarpd   -- libavl, libumem, libidspace, libnvpair, libmd, librename
  * libdladm   -- libdevinfo, libinetutil, libsocket, libscf, librcm,
                  libnvpair, libexacct, libkstat, libpool, libvarpd
  * libdlpi    -- libc, libinetutil, libdladm
  * libuuid    -- libsocket, libnsl, libc, libdlpi
  * libzonecfg -- the above plus libsec, libsecdb, libbsm, libproc, libpool,
                  libscf, libsysevent, libuutil, libxml2

and none of it can be skipped by linking alone, because GNU ld resolves each
shared object's own `DT_NEEDED` list along the runtime search path:
svcs -> libzonecfg -> libuuid -> libdlpi -> libdladm is a hard chain.

Note one trap for whoever does build it. `libzonecfg`'s `OBJECTS` includes
`definit.o`, whose source is `usr/src/common/definit/definit.c` -- outside
the library's own directory, reached through a `pics/%.o: $(SRC)/common/definit/%.c`
rule, and with nothing in `LDLIBS` to hint at it. That is the recurring
"one library deeper than the Makefile advertises" pattern; `libexacct` hid
`common/exacct` and `libproc` hid `common/list` the same way. Treat the list
above as a floor.

What retires this patch: packaging libzonecfg. That is expected to happen for
an unrelated reason rather than for `svcs` -- `libdladm` is the expensive node
in the chain and is wanted independently for `dladm`/`ipadm` once there is a
network stack to configure. When it is built for that, `svcs` should drop this
patch and link `-lzonecfg` properly.

Assisted-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/svc/svcs/Makefile b/usr/src/cmd/svc/svcs/Makefile
index 5592c76..8221cd4 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/svc/svcs/Makefile
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/svc/svcs/Makefile
@@ -34,7 +34,12 @@ include ../../Makefile.cmd
 include ../../Makefile.ctf
 
 POFILE =	$(PROG)_all.po
-LDLIBS +=	-lcontract -lscf -luutil -lumem -lnvpair -lzonecfg -lproc
+#
+# -lzonecfg is omitted, and svcs.c's one use of it is compiled out behind
+# HAVE_LIBZONECFG.  Define HAVE_LIBZONECFG and add -lzonecfg back to restore
+# it; see the commit message for why this build does not.
+#
+LDLIBS +=	-lcontract -lscf -luutil -lumem -lnvpair -lproc
 CPPFLAGS += -I ../common
 
 CERRWARN += $(CNOWARN_UNINIT)
diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/svc/svcs/svcs.c b/usr/src/cmd/svc/svcs/svcs.c
index bae26d5..f1680ef 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/svc/svcs/svcs.c
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/svc/svcs/svcs.c
@@ -79,7 +79,9 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <strings.h>
 #include <time.h>
+#ifdef HAVE_LIBZONECFG
 #include <libzonecfg.h>
+#endif
 #include <zone.h>
 
 #ifndef TEXT_DOMAIN
@@ -364,7 +366,10 @@ int
 pg_get_single_val(scf_propertygroup_t *pg, const char *propname, scf_type_t ty,
     void *vp, size_t sz, uint_t flags)
 {
-	char *buf, root[MAXPATHLEN];
+	char *buf;
+#ifdef HAVE_LIBZONECFG
+	char root[MAXPATHLEN];
+#endif
 	size_t buf_sz;
 	int ret = -1, r;
 	boolean_t multi = B_FALSE;
@@ -473,10 +478,12 @@ out:
 	 * As a convenience, we're going to prepend the zone path to the
 	 * name of the log file.
 	 */
+#ifdef HAVE_LIBZONECFG
 	root[0] = '\0';
 	(void) zone_get_rootpath(g_zonename, root, sizeof (root));
 	(void) strlcat(root, vp, sizeof (root));
 	(void) snprintf(vp, sz, "%s", root);
+#endif
 
 	return (ret);
 }
-- 
